# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the real values.
#
# `.env` is ignored by git and must never be committed or pasted into a chat.
# This `.env.example` file IS committed, so it must only ever list key names —
# never real values.
#
# Only list the keys this project actually needs. Delete the guidance lines once
# the project has its own keys. A project with no secrets still keeps this file
# so the pattern is obvious to whoever works on it next.

# The app's own AI model access. OpenCode runs the swarm on its own model
# access, so a project only needs this if the app itself calls a model.
# The orchestrator consults it when it evaluates AI capabilities for the project.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Only if the project uses TypeSafe's structured decision model (Jev).
# See docs/CAPABILITIES.md.
# JEV_API_KEY=
